          "anchor": "return H",
          "code": "    # Preserve the original number of rows.  When the HNF algorithm\n    # drops zero rows (which can happen when the matrix is treated as\n    # row\u2011style via flips and transposes), the result no longer matches the\n    # input shape.  Pad the bottom of the matrix with zero rows so that the\n    # output has the same row count as the original matrix.\n    if H.shape[0] < M.shape[0]:\n        from sympy import Matrix\n        zero_rows = Matrix.zeros(M.shape[0] - H.shape[0], H.shape[1])\n        H = H.col_join(zero_rows)\n    return H",
          "reason": "Ensures hermite_normal_form does not unintentionally drop zero rows, fixing the bug where row\u2011style HNF via flips loses rows."
        }
